# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build output
#
# Bracketed initials because git matches case-sensitively even where Windows does not, and MSBuild
# has produced both spellings over the years.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
publish/
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.binlog
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- editors and tooling
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- models
#
# Every model is a file the user supplies, and none of them is ours to redistribute. Together they
# are about two gigabytes, and their licences range from MIT to AGPL — see docs/MODELS.md, which
# lists each one, where it comes from, and what its licence permits.
#
# The providers README is guidance rather than a payload, so it stays.
/models/*
!/models/providers/
/models/providers/*
!/models/providers/README.txt

# And by extension, anywhere at all. The rule above guards one directory; this guards the mistake
# of putting a model somewhere else — beside a project, in a scratch folder, wherever a download
# defaulted to. A 1.4 GB file committed by accident cannot be taken back out of a public history
# without rewriting it, so this is worth the redundancy.
#
# Note the absence of *.bin: src/PixelFlux.Core/Geo/gazetteer.bin is a committed source asset.
*.onnx
*.onnx.data
*.onnx_data
*.ort
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.pt
*.pth
*.tflite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fetched ONNX Runtime natives
#
# 40 MB extracted from a published NuGet package by tools/fetch_runtime.py. Reproducible, so it is
# fetched rather than committed. Runtime.targets is source and must stay.
/runtime/**/*.dll

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the test corpus
#
# 132 photographs, about 90 MB, downloaded from Wikimedia Commons by tools/fetch_test_album.py and
# tools/fetch_people_set.py. Not committed for two reasons: it is large, and the photographs are
# other people's work under a spread of Creative Commons terms. Reproducing it from a script keeps
# the attribution with the source rather than asking this repository to carry it.
/testdata/*
# The provenance travels even though the photographs do not: two small tab-separated files naming
# every image, its author and its licence. Without them the fetch scripts would reproduce a corpus
# nobody could attribute.
!/testdata/album/
/testdata/album/*
!/testdata/album/ATTRIBUTION.tsv
!/testdata/people/
/testdata/people/*
!/testdata/people/ATTRIBUTION.tsv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local library data
#
# A real library lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\PixelFlux and never belongs here, but a stray copy made
# while debugging would carry somebody's actual photographs and the descriptions written about
# them. Ignored so that cannot happen by accident.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/cache/

# Python bytecode from the tools/ scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
